Subject: [VOTE] KIP-1235: Correct the default min.insync.replicas to 2 for the
 __remote_log_metadata topic
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: multipart/alternative; boundary="00000000000055459f0642f59c4d"

--00000000000055459f0642f59c4d
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi all,

I=E2=80=99d like to initiate the vote for KIP-1235 right away as it=E2=80=
=99s a minor
change with minimal risk.

Summary:

Currently, __remote_log_metadata relies on the broker default for min.isr
(typically 1).
With min.isr=3D1 and factor=3D3, acknowledged writes can be lost if the lea=
der
crashes before replication completes, making remote data permanently
unreachable.
What's more, the similar topic: __transaction_state sets min.isr=3D2 via
transaction.state.log.min.isr.We should provide the same durability for
__remote_log_metadata.

Proposed Change:
Add one new broker config: remote.log.metadata.topic.min.isr (default: 2)
When creating __remote_log_metadata, TopicBasedRemoteLogMetadataManager
will set min.insync.replicas=3D2 at the topic level.

KIP WIKI:
https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1235%3A+Correct+the+d=
efault+min.insync.replicas+to+2+for+the+__remote_log_metadata+topic
Discussion Thread:
https://lists.apache.org/thread/016mjw3rrcqnt8475bxr3b3npm0t32xl
PR: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/20811

Looking forward to your feedback!

Thanks!

Regards
Jian

--00000000000055459f0642f59c4d--

