> Summary:
>=20
> Currently, __remote_log_metadata relies on the broker default for min.isr
> (typically 1).
> With min.isr=3D1 and factor=3D3, acknowledged writes can be lost if the le=
ader
> crashes before replication completes, making remote data permanently
> unreachable.
> What's more, the similar topic: __transaction_state sets min.isr=3D2 via
> transaction.state.log.min.isr.We should provide the same durability for
> __remote_log_metadata.
>=20
> Proposed Change:
> Add one new broker config: remote.log.metadata.topic.min.isr (default: 2)
> When creating __remote_log_metadata, TopicBasedRemoteLogMetadataManager
> will set min.insync.replicas=3D2 at the topic level.
>=20
> KIP WIKI:
