> >
> > Currently, __remote_log_metadata relies on the broker default for min.i=
sr
> > (typically 1).
> > With min.isr=3D1 and factor=3D3, acknowledged writes can be lost if the
> leader
> > crashes before replication completes, making remote data permanently
> > unreachable.
> > What's more, the similar topic: __transaction_state sets min.isr=3D2 vi=
a
> > transaction.state.log.min.isr.We should provide the same durability for
> > __remote_log_metadata.
> >
> > Proposed Change:
> > Add one new broker config: remote.log.metadata.topic.min.isr (default: =
2)
> > When creating __remote_log_metadata, TopicBasedRemoteLogMetadataManager
> > will set min.insync.replicas=3D2 at the topic level.
> >
> > KIP WIKI:
> >
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1235%3A+Correct+the=
+default+min.insync.replicas+to+2+for+the+__remote_log_metadata+topic
> > Discussion Thread:
> > https://lists.apache.org/thread/016mjw3rrcqnt8475bxr3b3npm0t32xl
> > PR: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/20811
> >
> > Looking forward to your feedback!
> >
> > Thanks!
> >
> > Regards
> > Jian
>

