Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-19883) Support Hierarchical Transactional
 Acknowledgments for Share Groups
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394

Shekhar Prasad Rajak created KAFKA-19883:
--------------------------------------------

             Summary: Support Hierarchical Transactional Acknowledgments fo=
r Share Groups
                 Key: KAFKA-19883
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19883
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: New Feature
          Components: clients, consumer, core
    Affects Versions: 4.1.0
            Reporter: Shekhar Prasad Rajak


Add transactional acknowledgment support to Kafka Share Groups to enable +*=
exactly-once read semantics*+ in distributed stream processing engines like=
 Apache Spark and Apache Flink.

=C2=A0

=C2=A0*Current Behavior:*
=C2=A0 Share Groups support only immediate acknowledgment mode where record=
s are permanently acknowledged as soon as consumer.acknowledge() is called.=
 This creates data loss scenarios in distributed streaming frameworks:

=C2=A0 1. Worker polls and acknowledges records to Kafka
=C2=A0 2. Records are permanently removed from Kafka
=C2=A0 3. Checkpoint/batch fails before writing to sink
=C2=A0 4. Records are lost (acknowledged but never reached sink)

=C2=A0 This prevents exactly-once semantics in Spark/Flink with Share Group=
s.

=C2=A0 *Expected Behavior:*
=C2=A0 Share Groups should support transactional acknowledgment mode where:

=C2=A0 1. Records are acknowledged within transactions
=C2=A0 2. Acknowledgments are pending until transaction commits
=C2=A0 3. Transaction rollback makes ALL records available for retry
=C2=A0 4. Enables atomic coordination with framework checkpoints/batches

=C2=A0 *Proposed Solution:*

=C2=A0 Implement hierarchical two-phase commit transactions:
{quote}=C2=A0 BatchTransaction (coordinator/driver level)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =E2=94=9C=E2=94=80 TaskTransaction1 (worker/executor level)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =E2=94=82 =C2=A0 =C2=A0=E2=94=9C=E2=94=80 acknowledge(record1=
, ACCEPT)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =E2=94=82 =C2=A0 =C2=A0=E2=94=9C=E2=94=80 acknowledge(record2=
, ACCEPT)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =E2=94=82 =C2=A0 =C2=A0=E2=94=94=E2=94=80 prepare() =E2=86=90=
 Phase 1
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =E2=94=82
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =E2=94=9C=E2=94=80 TaskTransaction2 (worker/executor level)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =E2=94=82 =C2=A0 =C2=A0=E2=94=9C=E2=94=80 acknowledge(record3=
, ACCEPT)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =E2=94=82 =C2=A0 =C2=A0=E2=94=94=E2=94=80 prepare() =E2=86=90=
 Phase 1
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =E2=94=82
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =E2=94=94=E2=94=80 commit() =E2=86=90 Phase 2: Atomically com=
mits all task transactions
{quote}
=C2=A0

=C2=A0 - Batch transactions (coordinator-level)
=C2=A0 - Task transactions (worker-level)
=C2=A0 - Records stay in Kafka until transaction commits
=C2=A0 - Rollback on failure =E2=86=92 no data loss

=C2=A0

=C2=A0 *API Changes:*

=C2=A0 New Consumer API:
=C2=A0 // Batch-level transaction
=C2=A0 BatchTransaction beginBatchTransaction(String batchTransactionId);
=C2=A0 void commitBatchTransaction(BatchTransaction txn, Duration timeout)=
=C2=A0
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 throws TimeoutException, TransactionException;
=C2=A0 void rollbackBatchTransaction(BatchTransaction txn);

=C2=A0 // Task-level transaction
=C2=A0 TaskTransaction beginTaskTransaction(BatchTransaction parent, String=
 taskId);
=C2=A0 void acknowledge(TaskTransaction txn, ConsumerRecord<K,V> record, Ac=
knowledgeType type);
=C2=A0 void prepareTaskTransaction(TaskTransaction txn);
=C2=A0 void commitTaskTransaction(TaskTransaction txn);
=C2=A0 void rollbackTaskTransaction(TaskTransaction txn);

=C2=A0 *New Configuration:*
=C2=A0 share.acknowledgement.mode=3Dtransactional =C2=A0# Default: explicit
=C2=A0 share.batch.transaction.timeout.ms=3D300000
=C2=A0 share.task.transaction.timeout.ms=3D120000
=C2=A0 share.transaction.commit.timeout.ms=3D30000
=C2=A0 share.transaction.auto.rollback=3Dtrue

=C2=A0

*Target Use Cases:* Apache Spark structured streaming, Apache Flink exactly=
-once checkpoints, any coordinator-worker streaming framework.



