Thanks!

jian fu <fujian1115@gmail.com> =E4=BA=8E2025=E5=B9=B411=E6=9C=885=E6=97=A5=
=E5=91=A8=E4=B8=89 14:54=E5=86=99=E9=81=93=EF=BC=9A

> Hi everyone,
>
> I'd like to start a discussion on KIP-1235, a small change to set
> min.isr=3D2 for the __remote_log_metadata topic.
>
> KIP:
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1235%3A+Correct+the=
+default+min.insync.replicas+to+2+for+the+__remote_log_metadata+topic
>
> Problem:
>
> Currently, __remote_log_metadata relies on the broker default for min.isr
> (typically 1).
> With min.isr=3D1 and factor=3D3, acknowledged writes can be lost if the l=
eader
> crashes before replication
> completes, making remote data permanently unreachable.
>
> What's more, the similar topic: __transaction_state sets min.isr=3D2 via
> transaction.state.log.min.isr.
> We should provide the same durability for __remote_log_metadata.
>
>
> Proposed Change:
>
> Add one new broker config: remote.log.metadata.topic.min.isr (default: 2)
>
> When creating __remote_log_metadata, TopicBasedRemoteLogMetadataManager
> will set
> min.insync.replicas=3D2 at the topic level. The change only affects new
> clusters enabling Tiered Storage. Existing topics are unchanged.
>
>
> Looking forward to your feedback!
>
> Best regards,
> Jian
>

