> After tracing the failures, the root cause was narrowed down to commit=C2=
=A0[https://github.com/apache/kafka/commit/87657fdfc721055835f5b1f22151c461=
e85eab4a]. This change introduced a new try/catch around=C2=A0{{handleCompl=
etedAcknowledgements()}}=C2=A0in=C2=A0{{{}ShareConsumerImpl.java{}}}. The s=
ide effect is that all exceptions coming from the commit callback =E2=80=94=
 including GroupMaxSizeReachedException =E2=80=94 are now swallowed and onl=
y logged, preventing the test from ever receiving the exception.
>  - If the ack callback fires while {{poll()}}=C2=A0is executing =E2=86=92=
 exception is caught & swallowed =E2=86=92 test times out
>  - If the callback fires outside that path =E2=86=92 exception escapes =
=E2=86=92 test passes
> So the same test randomly passes/fails depending on scheduling of the ack=
 callback.
> Also, the test testAcknowledgementCommitCallbackThrowsException has been =
marked as Flaky for the same Root cause.



