Hi, Tom,

Thanks for the reply.

JR1. "Specifically, we propose adding new header fields to the
DefaultRecordBatch class to store the S3 path/location."

This feels unnatural. Could you explain why this is needed? For cost
optimization, we just need to ensure cost savings in the common case. We
don't need to add more complexity to optimize costs for infrequent cases.

JR2. "However, regarding the cost optimizations we discussed previously
(specifically the Intra-AZ Replicator for the read path and the Combined
Object logic for the producer/write path), we propose moving these
mechanisms to a separate KIP."

I think we need to get the replica assignment right in this KIP. Otherwise,
we won't achieve the goal of this KIP, which is saving cross-AZ network
cost.

Finally, I feel what's being proposed in the KIP is just a short-term,
stop-gap solution compared with KIP-1150, which provides more benefits. If
we are making progress on KIP-1150, it might not be worth pursuing this KIP
in parallel.

Jun

