> Using RF=3D1 is more about wanting to avoid replicating data at the Kafka
> Layer. In fact, object storage makes it easier to scale reads, such as by
> adding some read-only replicas. There is no replication semantics; instea=
d,
> it leverages the shared properties of object storage to improve fan-out.
