I'd like to give an update on progress for KIP-932 and KIP-1226. Today has be=
en challenging because of build failures on account of an OOM in the client u=
nit tests. We have now identified the troublesome commit and just merged a fi=
x.

PRs for 3 of the remaining 5 subtasks for KIP-932 (https://issues.apache.org/=
jira/browse/KAFKA-16092) are ready but the build problems thwarted their comp=
letion. This is one code fix, a PR to mark interfaces as stable, and document=
ation. That leaves 1 subtask (https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-175=
41) which should complete this week, and another (https://issues.apache.org/j=
ira/browse/KAFKA-19865) which is documenting metrics.

The final task for KIP-1226 has an approved PR which again has been hampered =
today by the builds.

I wonder whether you could postpone cutting the release branch by one day unt=
il the morning of 21st. If not, we can cherry-pick, but I thought I'd ask.

Thanks,
Andrew

