    Fix Version/s: 4.2.0
       Resolution: Fixed

> Failures in the StateUpdater thread may lead to inability to shut down a stream thread
> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-19831
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-19831
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Bug
>          Components: streams
>    Affects Versions: 3.8.0
>            Reporter: Nikita Shupletsov
>            Assignee: Nikita Shupletsov
>            Priority: Major
>             Fix For: 4.2.0
>
>         Attachments: StateUpdaterFailureIntegrationTest.patch
>
>
> If during rebalance a failure occurs in the StateUpdater thread, and this failure leads to the thread shutdown, the Stream thread may get into an infinite wait state during it's shutdown.
> See the attached test that reproduces the issue.



