   @mingyen066 This may be a bigger lift, but I believe Gradle supports decoupling the JDK used for invoking Gradle from the JDK used for compiling the project code, via the "toolchains" concept. https://docs.gradle.org/current/userguide/toolchains.html#toolchains
   
   Maybe it would be worth looking at that for trunk too, it could enable Kafka to upgrade the JDK faster in the future, even before Gradle gains support?
   
   Anyway, just an idea, not sure if it's worth doing?


