            Assignee: sanghyeok An


Kafka Streams throws a ClassCastException when using different Consumed ins=
tances for the same topic.

For example:

builder.stream("A", Consumed.with(Serdes.String(), Serdes.String()))
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0.peek((k, v) -> System.out.println(k));
builder.stream("A", Consumed.with(Serdes.ByteArray(), Serdes.ByteArray()))
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0.peek((k, v) -> System.out.println(k));

=C2=A0

Since both use the same topic name and the same ConsumedInternal configurat=
ion for auto offset reset, these two StreamSourceNodes are merged during to=
pology building.

=C2=A0

As a result, the Topology is built successfully.

=C2=A0

However, when the StreamThread starts, the consumer begins to receive recor=
ds from the broker, and the records flow through the pipeline, a ClassCastE=
xception is thrown at runtime.

=C2=A0

In my opinion, we have two options:
 # Document this behavior.
 # When merging source nodes, the builder should consider the full Consumed=
Internal configuration (for example, key/value SerDes and timestamp extract=
or), instead of only the auto offset reset policy.

=C2=A0

I think option 1 is also acceptable, because Kafka Streams will fail fast w=
ith a ClassCastException before the consumer commits any offsets.

=C2=A0

Option 2 would require more substantial changes in Kafka Streams, because T=
imestampExtractor and key/value SerDes do not expose a straightforward way =
to check semantic equivalence.



--
